A||||23||Jasons85GT||Sh*t! (Please help, im only 17)||||8||
Z||000000||Jasons85GT||10-12-2001||04:26 PM||||Ok, i recently bought an 85 2.8 GT from a good friend. Well maintained, and runs great! Love it! Well, I go outside today to check the oil, and its this greenish color! Not too bad, but green! I immediately started cursing! Ok, im thinking water leak?? What do yall think? Any replies are appreciated! Thanks...||||reg||8
Z||000001||sqoach||10-12-2001||04:32 PM||||Sounds like a bad head gasket leak to me. Usually the oil would be just a milky brown color. If it's green, something must be pretty bad. How's your coolant level? Does it run hot?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||11
Z||000002||JohnF||10-12-2001||04:34 PM||||Yes, it is bad!  Water is getting in the crankcase from somewhere.  A blown head gasket is the most likely cause but it can come from lots of places (cracked/warped head, cracked block, etc).  Hope it is a "simple" head gasket.||||reg||8
Z||000003||fix||10-12-2001||05:37 PM||||Even if this is just a "simple head gasket" problem, you are in for a complete tear down if you want to do it right.  The mainbearings in your engine don't like anti-freeze and if you simply replace the head gasket most likely the engine will develop some undesirable noise when you get it back together.  I've heard this from people who have actually had it happen, so I don't think I'd take any chances.  It's better to fix it once and do it right than it is to fix it twice because you went the cheap route first.  Just my opinion.<P>------------------<BR>"If it doesn't scare you, it's not fast enough."||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||10-12-2001||05:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jasons85GT:<BR><B>Ok, i recently bought an 85 2.8 GT from a good friend. Well maintained, and runs great! Love it! Well, I go outside today to check the oil, and its this greenish color! Not too bad, but green! I immediately started cursing! Ok, im thinking water leak?? What do yall think? Any replies are appreciated! Thanks...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Before ya blow a gasket (pun intended!), is the oil watery, like it has water mixed in?<BR>Ask your friend what type of oil he ran, it may be normal...<BR>Normally, if antifreeze gets into the oil, it gets frothy and brown colored, like a cappuchino...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||jfuredy||10-12-2001||06:28 PM||||Aren't some oil leak detecting additives fluorescent green?  As Fierowrecker asked, if it's still an oily consistency, and not milky this might be what it is.<P>I guess an easy way to test it would be to change the oil and drive it a SHORT time to get it up to operating temp and see if it turns green again, or if it is OK.<P>You should also drain your coolant system and check for signs of oil in there.<P>Just my two cents,<BR>Joe Furedy<BR>'88 Formula<BR>Phoenix, AZ||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnF||10-12-2001||07:03 PM||||Ah! yes,  FIX is right.  There is no such thing as "simple problem" in the crankcase!. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||btoth||10-12-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fix:<BR><B>Even if this is just a "simple head gasket" problem, you are in for a complete tear down if you want to do it right.  The mainbearings in your engine don't like anti-freeze and if you simply replace the head gasket most likely the engine will develop some undesirable noise when you get it back together.  I've heard this from people who have actually had it happen, so I don't think I'd take any chances.  It's better to fix it once and do it right than it is to fix it twice because you went the cheap route first.  Just my opinion.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're right!  My head gaskets completely went one night and the engine wouldn't start.  After having it rebuilt (from the heads up), a year later my engine started knocking... bearings where starting to go... no oil pressure... not good.  That's why I now have a new engine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hopefully you just have a tiny leak.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||10-12-2001||07:46 PM||||The only oil I've had that was green was automatic transmission oil from B&M.  It was a surprize when I first started to pour it down the funnel. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||10-12-2001||08:13 PM||||Oil and coolant makes milky brown gravy, it,s not green. Sounds like it might be the type oil like Fierowrecker says.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pike||10-12-2001||09:52 PM||||Don't listen to anyone telling you ya got water in your oil dude. They know about as much as you do. Oil is green right out of the can man...don't you know that? hahahaha! Water in oil will give you a milky brown gooop! <P>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000011||Sootah||10-12-2001||10:16 PM||||OH MY GOD!!! I have (I think) the same problem!! Here's the story:<BR>I went to pick up my 90,000 mile 85 GT this last Wednesday. Get there, pay guy, drive off. Running great. Go to gas station, as filling up get some guy chatting me up and complements the hell out of the car (Big ole ego boost, only owned the car 5 min) Get on the freeway from vegas and notice that the car seems kinda wobbly. Front right tire needs a bit of air. I pull off at a station and notice this knock/tick like noise coming from the engine bay. I think great, I've just bought the car and I'm already gonna throw a rod.. Well; Turns out that while the sound is related to engine RPM it's not quite directly so. We figure maybe an odd exaust leak. Get back on freeway and about 2 miles down the road the temp starts to rise quickly. I pull off just as she overheats; turn it off and watch the radiator boil over. At this time I am thinking that I merely didn't have enough coolant in there (we didn't check it b4 we left) so we add that and left again. As soon as I am on the freeway the 'check engine' light comes on. I pull off, and turn off the car. I then have my friend drive the car. I follow in his. As I am following I see steam and smoke and crap bellowing out of the engine bay. I pull him over and he said that as he was going along that the noise suddendly went whiiiir-thump and then the car started running smoothly. Once again I am thinking aww, damnint! I've thrown a rod!<P>We got the car towed back here yesterday. There is no exit wound for the rod. The oil is full. The car still runs (Kinda noisy, but quite well). It does steam like a *****  though.<P>Sorry that was so long. What do you think is up?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
Z||000012||btoth||10-13-2001||12:18 AM||||When I pulled my heads off... the coolant wasn't even completely mixed with the oil.  It looked as if it had seperated.  You could clearly make out the little green pools mixed in with the brown yukky looking oil.<P>I dont know if I would've been able to tell from just checking my dipstick.<P>Does the car smoke at all when you first turn it on?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Sootah||10-13-2001||12:29 AM||||Havent watched it when I very first turn it on. Will have to wait till morning to see that. So you guys do think its a blown head gasket?<P>Letcha know first thing in the morning.<P>-<B><I>Sootah</I></B>||||reg||5
Z||000014||gt boy||10-13-2001||12:38 AM||||i used to use a oil called Motul in all my motorcycles..it was green out of the bottle untill i got burnt up in the motor...then it went brown.  i must admit it was awsome oil.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mach10||10-13-2001||01:45 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> All the oil I've EVER used comes a nice honey color... ||||reg||5
Z||000016||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||03:02 PM||||Ive bought an oil in Oklahoma before called Blue Velvet, and it was as blue as the ocean. Before i do anything, Id drain the oil and add new filter and oil and see what happens. if it is messed up your only out $8-$10. also check your radiator and overflow tank to make sure there clean and full (no oily residue)||||reg||1
Z||000017||Sootah||10-13-2001||04:50 PM||||-K-, I have a parts car. If this turns out to be a cracked head (I am operating under the assumption that it is in the head somewhere right now) could I use the one off of my 85/86 parts car? I ask because its been sitting there for <I>ever</I> and it looks like hell. However, I'd imagine that the head would be fine for refurbishing even if the engine is all seized from sitting. Correct?<P>Oh, I'm gonna go see if the black beauty smokes on startup.||||reg||5
Z||000018||btoth||10-13-2001||04:58 PM||||Chances are, your head is not cracked.  Try the oil change first... just drive it around like normal, check the oil after a while and see if it turns greenish again.  If it does, then it's probably just your gasket(s).  I do believe that the V6 heads are the same btw.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Sootah||10-13-2001||04:58 PM||||Teeny puff of white-ish smoke on start up. Idles slighly rough, but pretty well. Didn't rev it. Looked in the engine bay as it was running and couldn't see smoke coming from anywhere.<P>Going to do a compression test as well as drain the oil and see what she is like. Now to get to the crankcase all you have to do is take off the oil pan, right? Is it feasible to give her a good ole fashioned overhaul while still in the engine bay (If she needs it)?||||reg||1
Z||000020||fix||10-13-2001||06:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt boy:<BR><B>i used to use a oil called Motul in all my motorcycles..it was green out of the bottle untill i got burnt up in the motor...then it went brown.  i must admit it was awsome oil.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ummm, those motorcycles wouldn't be 2 strokes by any chance would they?  2-stroke oil is green||||reg||1
Z||000021||Sootah||10-13-2001||07:53 PM||||SON OF A FÜCKING ***** !!!!!!! IT IS A ROD!!!!!! The damned exit wound is merele <I>hiding</I> on the backside next to the oil filter!! AHHH!!! So, how much is <B><I>this</I></B> going to cost me to find an engine and put in??? Shìt!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000022||Old Lar||10-13-2001||08:44 PM||||Cost will depend on what you want to spend.<BR>Check the Fiero Web ring for a Fiero club in the Virginia area.  They may be able to help you find a decent 2.8.  Most of the guys with engines that I know of are not in Virginia.  Bob Parker's Kick Hill Farms is in Conneticutt,  Ed Park's Fiero Factory in in Alabama, Twin Lakes Fiero is in Illinois.<P>Of course if you have ~$4K you could get a new crate engine installed, or for less than half that amount, get a remanufactured engine and install it yourself.<P>I feel your pain.  I've had two engines put into my 88.  I'd really like to find the previous owner and tell him the car only needed a tune up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Old Lar||10-13-2001||08:44 PM||||Cost will depend on what you want to spend.<BR>Check the Fiero Web ring for a Fiero club in the Virginia area.  They may be able to help you find a decent 2.8.  Most of the guys with engines that I know of are not in Virginia.  Bob Parker's Kick Hill Farms is in Conneticutt,  Ed Park's Fiero Factory in in Alabama, Twin Lakes Fiero is in Illinois.<P>Of course if you have ~$4K you could get a new crate engine installed, or for less than half that amount, get a remanufactured engine and install it yourself.<P>I feel your pain.  I've had two engines put into my 88.  I'd really like to find the previous owner and tell him the car only needed a tune up.<BR>||||reg||1
